+# Proposal
+
+## Why
+
+Deleting a customer currently makes the admin order APIs unable to retrieve that customer's historical orders, even though order records are required for support and retention. The admin order list also loses pagination after its first page, preventing staff from finding older orders.
+
+## What Changes
+
+- Preserve order records and their customer-independent checkout details when a customer account is deleted.
+- Allow an admin to retrieve a preserved order, including billing, delivery, placed-with email, history, transactions, and status operations, with no attached customer when the account no longer exists.
+- List orders by a deleted customer id without requiring the customer row to exist, returning newest-first results and accurate totals.
+- Correct admin order filtering and pagination so every requested zero-based page returns its matching slice with accurate `recordsTotal` and `totalPages`.
+- Ensure a newly registered account using a deleted account's email is distinct and does not inherit historical orders.
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### New Capabilities
+- `order-retention`: Retain and administer orders independently of customer account lifetime, including historical lookup and paginated admin browsing.
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+
+## Impact
+
+- Order/customer persistence mappings and delete behavior in `sm-core`.
+- Order repository/service criteria, sorting, count, and pagination logic in `sm-core`.
+- Admin order API and facade/populators in `sm-shop`.
+- Regression and integration tests covering deletion, re-registration, detail retrieval, customer-id lookup, and page navigation.
