+# Tasks
+
+## 1. Preserve order data independently of customers
+
+- [x] 1.1 Update customer/order persistence mappings and customer deletion behavior so deleting a customer does not delete or invalidate orders, and verify with a persistence regression test that the order remains addressable by id.
+- [x] 1.2 Make order detail and order-list population null-safe for a missing customer while retaining order-owned email, billing, delivery, history, and transaction data, and verify with API/facade tests for a deleted customer.
+
+## 2. Implement historical customer-id lookup and admin paging
+
+- [x] 2.1 Update order repository/service criteria queries to filter directly by stored customer id, apply all admin filters before paging, sort newest first, and return full matching counts and ceiling page totals; verify repository/service tests for page 0, later pages, empty results, and out-of-range pages.
+- [x] 2.2 Update the private customer-order endpoint to accept a missing customer row and return historical orders with accurate `recordsTotal`, and verify endpoint tests for deleted ids and ids with no orders.
+- [x] 2.3 Verify the private order detail, status update, history, and payment transaction endpoints continue to work for preserved orders, including accurate pagination metadata for filtered admin order lists.
+
+## 3. Protect account re-registration boundaries
+
+- [x] 3.1 Add an integration regression test that deletes an account, registers the same email as a new account, and verifies the new customer id sees none of the old customer id's orders while the old orders remain available to admins.
+- [x] 3.2 Run the relevant module test suites and validate the OpenSpec change with `openspec validate preserve-orders-after-customer-deletion --type change`.
+
+## Workflow follow-up
+
+- Archive the completed OpenSpec change after implementation and verification.
